message: "If you use this workflow in research, teaching or a product, please cite it as below."
title: "incremental-work-order: a dispatch workflow for long-running coding agents"
abstract: >-
  A repository-backed dispatch process for long-running agent work: one main tree schedules, each sub-tree
  executes its own slice of work orders, batches end in git checkpoints that are inspection windows rather than
  stops, and merges back are approval-gated and re-verified on the main tree. It ships the rules, templates, a
  structural validator, an anti-false-green checklist and behavioural eval cases.
type: software
